// Functions errcheck should not report, each with the convention it encodes.
// See the `lint` target in the Makefile for the longer reasoning.

// Writing to the terminal a CLI is already reporting through. There is
// nothing to do with the error, and checking it would double every command
// body. This was 315 of the original 325 findings.
fmt.Fprintf
fmt.Fprint
fmt.Fprintln

// Read-path cleanup in a defer: the rows are already drained or the query
// already failed, and there is no caller left to return to.
(*database/sql.Rows).Close
(*database/sql.Conn).Close
(*database/sql.DB).Close

// Rollback after a successful Commit is a documented no-op; several call
// sites already say so inline.
(*database/sql.Tx).Rollback

// Closing a file the process only READ. The write path is deliberately NOT
// excluded and must stay checked: internal/audit/jsonl.FileSink.Close
// returns its error to callers who act on it, because a dropped Close there
// silently loses buffered audit records -- which is the one case where this
// whole category stops being cosmetic.
(*os.File).Close
